WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
- What was the moment you knew
you had to dedicate your life

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.440
to working with chimpanzees?

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.200
- Well, first of all, it was Africa.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.620
I read Tarzan of the Apes
and fell in love with him.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.816
And I was very jealous,
he married the wrong Jane.

00:00:13.816 --> 00:00:16.170
(audience and guests laughing)

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.003
- He really did.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.866
- So that was when my
dream of Africa began.

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:23.790
I grow up, go to Africa,
live with wild animals

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.440
and write books about them.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.840
And everybody laughed, except, again, mom,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.120
she said if you really want
to do something like this,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.350
you'll have to work really hard.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.343
Take advantage of every opportunity.

00:00:33.343 --> 00:00:36.180
And if you don't get up,
hopefully you find a way.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.730
Which I've spread that around the world,

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.760
especially in disadvantaged communities.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.220
And so many people have
said, Jane, thank you.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.290
You taught me because
you followed your dream,

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.120
I can follow mine.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:48.953
So anyway,

00:00:48.953 --> 00:00:50.700
I got out there.
- Absolutely. It's inspiring.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.830
- Yes, I met Dr. Leakey.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.830
I would've studied any
animal to be in nature

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.290
and he offered me the one most like us.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.450
I mean, it's like fate, isn't it?

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.610
It was meant to be.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.520
And so chimpanzees, I was sent off to be

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.240
the first person ever
to study chimpanzees.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.073
- That's incredible.

00:01:10.073 --> 00:01:12.839
So did you have anything
you wanted to ask Dr. Jane?

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.010
- No, I'm just,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.980
I hope I can be a mom like your mom was.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.360
It's really inspiring

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.550
because all of the things
that you said, it's true.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.160
Like our instincts are to go,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.960
oh, don't do that, it's messy.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.930
But in reality, all of
those little things,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.513
they really do form a person.

